  "title": "Kodera2023: Left/right-hand motor-imagery EEG dataset",
  "description": "A left/right-hand motor-imagery EEG dataset from 29 healthy participants recorded at the University of West Bohemia. Participants performed cue-based single-class imagery of left- or right-hand movement over four runs. EEG was recorded in BrainVision format with a standard 10-20 montage. The dataset is a BIDS re-release produced with MOABB for brain-computer interface research.",
  "methods_description": "Cue-based single-class left- or right-hand motor imagery with visual cues, 4 s trials, and 4 runs per session. EEG was recorded with BrainVision Recorder (BrainProducts) at 500 Hz using 9 channels (Fz, Cz, Pz, F3, F4, P3, P4, C3, C4) in a standard 10-20 montage, with 50 Hz line frequency.",
